title a lantern twice becomes a loom, and the card read the wrong half
prompt Keaton said kg the fold loom -- the tool REDS %270 booked as the next lap's own.
think %270 specified it exactly: re-anchor a moved row's `](../` to `](../../`, leave `](../REDS.md)` alone, name the shelf. Reading the pin first found a second class the spec had not named -- `](archive/NAME)` points from construction/ into the shelf directory and would resolve to archive/archive/NAME from a shelf. No row carries that form today, so handling it is prevention, and it costs one substitution.
think The loom is two pieces on purpose. A pure filter that re-anchors text, and a fold that moves named rows through it. The filter is the mechanism and is testable alone; the fold is the policy and carries every refusal.
think Five refusals, each because the fold would be wrong rather than untidy: a shelf whose basename lacks `rows-` is invisible to the monotone glob and reports a gap where the row stands; a shelf that does not exist wants its header written by a person, since which rows and what they taught together is meaning rather than bytes; an absent row is a typo or an already-folded row and both want an eye; an OPEN row belongs on the pin; and a fold past twelve rows means somebody meant to move the page.
think Run against the real ledger the loom refused every row on the pin, because all four still read OPEN. That is the right answer rather than a gap -- this round had already hand-folded the closed ones.
obs The control caught a defect in my own control code: `grep -c` prints 0 and exits 1, so `|| echo 0` appended a second zero and the comparison read `0\n0`. The same shape sat in the tool. Both repaired; the control earning its keep on the lap it was written.
obs Then grading the new tools opened a red. Two came back C and one B with `register=100`, and that combination cannot happen to real prose -- a page that leads perfectly with what is does not also read at postgraduate length. `qa_report_card.sh` skips every line whose first non-whitespace is `#`, which is right for Markdown headings and exactly inverted for a program, where `#` and `//` open the only prose the file has. Reach read 209 words of shell code and returned a reading grade of 86 against a ceiling of 9, flooring Reach at zero.
obs Booked as REDS %276 and repaired in the same lap: the card classifies the artifact once, ahead of both readings, and feeds a program its comment lines with the marker stripped and the shebang dropped. Markdown readings are byte-identical, checked on three pages across all three settings, and the card's own sixty-seven-behavior witness still passes.
obs The sibling `prose_register_scan.sh` needed nothing, and measuring said so: its roster is `*.md` plus four named root documents, so the markdown rule is correct in its own domain. The fault lived only where the card widened the input past what the rule was written for -- worth checking rather than assuming, since the two carry the same line.
obs Second instrument fault in one day, after `docs/COMPASS.md` read C at door for being a pointer card. A meter pointed at a class of artifact it was never shaped for reports a fault in the artifact, and a card that manufactures a fault invites a repair that makes the artifact worse.
loom reds_fold_control cases=23 refusals=11 welcomes=12
loom qa_report_card before_repair="grade 86 vs ceiling 9, reach 0" after_repair="grade 8 and 9 vs ceiling 9"
file tools/fixtures/reds_fold_reanchor.sh the filter -- both link classes, the pin's own pointer held
file tools/fixtures/reds_fold.sh the fold -- five named refusals, twelve-row bound, inode-preserving writes
file tools/fixtures/reds_fold_control.sh twenty-three behaviors on planted trees, both directions
file tools/r/reds_fold_witness.rish three readings: the control, the living shelves, the standing catch
file tools/fixtures/qa_report_card.sh REDS %276 -- one classification ahead of both readings
file construction/REDS.md %276 booked and closed; the spine reads 276
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the loom's witness seated
recommend keep-going -- the loom stands and refuses correctly, so the next fold costs no care; `readlink -f` four sites and `sed -i` four remain mechanical, and the rune renames plus the derived-spine key stay at Keaton's door.
